{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1356950-vtr-2e-v5-reducing-dice-rolling-on-agains","id":1356950,"title":"[VtR 2e / V5] Reducing dice rolling on Agains","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-25T16:09:44-08:00","id":1356950,"title":"[VtR 2e / V5] Reducing dice rolling on Agains","content":"hey there!<br /> <br /> i'm looking to simplify some things and am trying to reduce dice rolling at the table.<br /> <br /> i'm thinking of dropping Again rules and replacing them with V5's doubles rule.<br /> <br /> for example, instead of 10-Again, every two 10s would equal four successes. the same would apply for 9-Agains, and such.<br /> <br /> problem is, i have no mind for statistics and don't know what this would do to percentage of success at the table. would this achieve my goals? would it help? hurt? destroy life as we know it?<br /> <br /> any insight would be most appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T16:25:11-08:00","id":1356951,"title":"","content":"I can run a Monte Carlo analysis later, but off the top of my head, it seems like it would increase the average number of successes and make big pools even better.<br /> <br /> My quick, informal reasoning: right now, on average, a 10 is worth 1.333\u2026 successes. In this system, on average, a 10 would be worth a bit less than 2 successes (since you sometimes don't have another 10 to pair it with). This would also give you an extra advantage to having a large pool, since having more dice increases the odds of a second 10 to pair it with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T16:26:11-08:00","id":1356952,"title":"","content":"(That said, is rolling up 10s really taking that much time? I've found my players enjoy it, because it makes rolling a 10 more viscerally satisfying.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T16:35:32-08:00","id":1356953,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm just trying to streamline things, to keep things moving and focused on the story and less on mechanics. For example, I'm also going to try using Hunger Dice instead of the Blood Pool. I'm trying to get as much done in single rolls as I can so we can move back to the story. If I can't find something that works, I can always default to the RAW.<br /> <br /> I'm also happily open to suggestions. If you find this idea to be too disruptive to outcomes, how would you go about trying to achieve the same Successful Oomph from Agains without the extra rolling?<br /> <br /> Thanks for taking the time!<br /> <br /> *edit* ya know, maybe i'm going about this backwards. so, i like a lot of the base rule adjustments in V5. i just don't want to play Masq.<br /> <br /> maybe instead of trying to backport fundamental rules, maybe i should just try a V5 base except with Requiem Clans and Disciplines, with no Generation? i'm not sure, but that's sort of what i'm grappling with, trying to meld V5 and VtR 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 12-25-2019, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T17:26:52-08:00","id":1356959,"title":"","content":"The V5 method adds a completely unnecessary step in needing pairs. It's easier on the math and players to just have 10s count as two successes.<br /> <br /> By itself, there isn't a huge problem, however you're massively skewing the statistical values of different options. The math of the CofD systems are built around 3 dice averaging 1 success, changing it to 2.5 dice averaging 1 success means everything's value changes. Dice adders give you more, exceptional successes become easier, systems that require specific numbers of successes (like inflicting Stun) are going to come up more, etc.<br /> <br /> The biggest question is how much of the rest of the system are you willing to retool for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T18:34:47-08:00","id":1356965,"title":"","content":"Right, right, I get ya. So, what's the difference between every 10 counting twice and the V5 method, statistically? Why did they add the extra step?<br /> <br /> I'm certainly open to just counting Agains twice, I just want to be careful of the implications.<br /> <br /> I'm not really looking to rework everything. I'm willing to accept a little variance overall toward more or less success, as long as it's not extreme variance.<br /> <br /> Also, while I generally like much of V5, i don't want to go back to TN 6. I prefer the 30% of TN 8 in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T18:39:58-08:00","id":1356966,"title":"","content":"For large enough pools, the difference (between tens count double and paired tens count double) doesn't matter. It's only relevant for small pools, where it makes explosions less likely.<br /> <br /> Also, Arms put it well\u2014if it's a tradeoff between &quot;players roll more dice when they get a big success&quot; and &quot;players do more mental math when they get a big success&quot;, I'm going to stick with the former.<br /> <br /> (P.S. Have you looked at Atrocity Dice? They're an optional mechanic from one of the between-editions Requiem books, and are what V5's Hunger Dice are based on.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T18:40:32-08:00","id":1356967,"title":"","content":"The difference between every 10 counting twice and V5 is...slight. Counting 10s twice, being more reliable, is more meaningful at smaller dice pools, but once they get big enough it's very small.<br /> <br /> Why? From what I understand it's an artifact of the concept that lead to Messy Crits with the pairing of a Hunger 10 and a normal 10 for a special effect before things like how WP would work was settled on.<br /> <br /> The level of variance... well.. depends. For basic rolls without Merits/powers and so on... it's not that big. But the more additional permutations that get applied the greater the variance becomes.<br /> <br /> Atrocity dice are in The Danse Macabre","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-25-2019, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T19:44:56-08:00","id":1356972,"title":"","content":"Great, thanks so much for this, all. So it sounds like I'd be fine just going for Agains count double. I just deferred to V5 since I'm not a pro designer and they seemed to be in the direction I want to go, but I figured people here could help elucidate things for me. So thanks!<br /> <br /> I vaguely recall Atrocity dice, but aren't they more for humanity and degeneration rather than hunger? Or are you saying I should look to adapting that to serve for Hunger?<br /> <br /> I'll go pull up my copy now and give a read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T14:29:48-08:00","id":1357110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicodemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1356950-vtr-2e-v5-reducing-dice-rolling-on-agains#post1356950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey there!<br /> <br /> i'm looking to simplify some things and am trying to reduce dice rolling at the table.<br /> <br /> i'm thinking of dropping Again rules and replacing them with V5's doubles rule.<br /> <br /> for example, instead of 10-Again, every two 10s would equal four successes. the same would apply for 9-Agains, and such.<br /> <br /> problem is, i have no mind for statistics and don't know what this would do to percentage of success at the table. would this achieve my goals? would it help? hurt? destroy life as we know it?<br /> <br /> any insight would be most appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>The double 10s is the method Exalted 3E uses also, so if you do move forward there is a lot of reference available for the dice mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T16:08:44-08:00","id":1357124,"title":"","content":"Ah, good to know, Graylion! Thanks! Yeah, I think I'll be moving forward with that.<br /> <br /> I'm navigating a few editions and games now as this is going to be a Requiem for Rome game, in VtR 2e, incorporating some base mechanics of V5 that I really appreciate (no gas tank, blood affinity, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T08:21:38-08:00","id":1357362,"title":"","content":"Why not make it every 2 10's add 1 success? This makes it far closer to the normally expected 1.33 (ignoring rolling 10-again on a re-rolled 10) successes per 10. Since if you roll exactly even 10's it'll be 1.5 for those 10's, but if you roll an uneven number then the last 10 you roll essentially becomes just &quot;1&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the average successes per 10 would depend on the amount of 10's you roll, and would be:<br /> (Amount of 10's : average successes/10)<br /> 1: 1<br /> 2: 1.5<br /> 3: 1.33<br /> 4: 1.5<br /> 5: 1.4<br /> <br /> Across these 5 scenario's that would average 1.346... of course some of these scenario's will be more likely than others, but on the whole I don't think it skews the math enough to really matter on the global scale.<br /> So you could do this to make the gameplay slightly faster, or you can re-roll to have that re-roll excitement some players like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-28-2019, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T09:54:23-08:00","id":1357372,"title":"","content":"ah that's an interesting middle ground!<br /> <br /> would you elucidate for me how it compares to just counting 10s twice? it's hard for me to envision the differences and impact.<br /> <br /> thanks for taking the time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T10:43:39-08:00","id":1357375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicodemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1356950-vtr-2e-v5-reducing-dice-rolling-on-agains?p=1357372#post1357372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ah that's an interesting middle ground!<br /> <br /> would you elucidate for me how it compares to just counting 10s twice? it's hard for me to envision the differences and impact.<br /> <br /> thanks for taking the time!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you count 10's twice then each 10 on 10-Again is worth 2 successes, which is a big difference up from ~1.33. Especially once you go up to 8-Again the total amount of successes will be a lot higher that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T11:35:30-08:00","id":1357380,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see I see, 1.3 successes per 10, assuming a successful reroll. I get it now, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T15:50:43-08:00","id":1358095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1356950-vtr-2e-v5-reducing-dice-rolling-on-agains?p=1356966#post1356966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Arms put it well\u2014if it's a tradeoff between &quot;players roll more dice when they get a big success&quot; and &quot;players do more mental math when they get a big success&quot;, I'm going to stick with the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been mulling this over a lot and I think i've come to agree with you. When you have a bunch of splayed out dice, I think the reroll is actually faster due to being simpler.<br /> <br /> Ok, so given that, may I ask a follow up question? How would that work with the presence of Hunger dice? Not for the Hunger dice themselves, they don't get rerolled, but how the #-Again mechanic works with Messy Crits.<br /> <br /> Namely, do the players HAVE to reroll? Or can they choose whether or not to reroll?<br /> <br /> Player gets 4 successes, two are tens, one of which is a Hunger 10. Does she HAVE to reroll the normal 10, pray to RNGesus that she doesn't Messy Crit? Or prepare to spend Willpower if she wants to re-roll up to three normal dice (ala V5?)<br /> <br /> Or maybe she can choose to not reroll, accept the normal success, restrain herself, and hold back the Beast.<br /> <br /> Or maybe she decides to go all in and risk it all for the thrill. She rerolls, get the Messy Crit, takes a Beat and revels in it.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 12-31-2019, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T16:57:16-08:00","id":1358106,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at Atrocity Dice? I like their mechanic better than V5's messy crits: in Requiem, the Beast is more &quot;competent predator&quot; than &quot;collateral damage at all costs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T18:42:29-08:00","id":1358119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1356950-vtr-2e-v5-reducing-dice-rolling-on-agains?p=1358106#post1358106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at Atrocity Dice? I like their mechanic better than V5's messy crits: in Requiem, the Beast is more &quot;competent predator&quot; than &quot;collateral damage at all costs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey!<br /> <br /> I like the Atrocity dice system, for sure. But here's my issue. It's all concerned with the Humanity and degeneration system, which I don't really mind at default, and not the hunger, blood and feeding system.<br /> <br /> If you're suggesting a way to have it function in connection with blood and feeding, I'm afraid I'm having a hard time seeing how to make that connection and bridge that gap. :/<br /> <br /> Do you have something in mind about how to start that process?<br /> <br /> I'll take another gander and see if something jumps out at me.<br /> <br /> *Edit* unless you're simply suggesting just keep the blood pool and vitae system as is, add the atrocity dice system and call it a day, since feeding is doing harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 12-31-2019, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T21:47:18-08:00","id":1358143,"title":"","content":"I'm suggesting using the consequences from Atrocity Dice coming up success rather than the consequences from V5's Hunger Dice coming up 10, because V5 has a very different view of the Beast: it's a malevolent force working against the character and trying to cause as much damage as possible if it gets free, rather than a careful predator that's fundamentally part of the character's own mind.<br /> <br /> In Requiem, the Beast is subtle and competent and will generally achieve its goals (just in an inhuman, amoral way), while in V5 it's meant to be a hindrance, never a help\u2014see how the default consequence of a Messy Critical, if no other case applies, is to <i>turn it into a dramatic failure</i> as the Beast just fucks everything up. In other words, when the V5 Beast gets the absolute best result it can possibly get, it's by default a dram-fail for the character. The Requiem Beast on the other hand generally gets you what you want\u2014if you're hungry you get blood, if you're in danger you get away, etc\u2014it just achieves its goal without caring about your Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 01-01-2020, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T08:03:07-08:00","id":1358196,"title":"","content":"aaahhh, i get where you're coming from now. yeah, i'm totally amenable to that! ok, i'll take a look and see what i can see.<br /> <br /> thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T11:57:21-08:00","id":1358459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1356950-vtr-2e-v5-reducing-dice-rolling-on-agains?p=1358143#post1358143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suggesting using the consequences from Atrocity Dice coming up success rather than the consequences from V5's Hunger Dice coming up 10</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so let's put aside the V5 messy crits and beastial failures.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Atrocity dice section, it states on p167 that Atrocity dice taint your actions when a ten is rolled on them, with severity increasing for each ten. So I could go with that for the Hunger dice, with maybe a frenzy on a chance Hunger die 1? Maybe also on an exceptional success with a Hunger 10 (a Beastial Success, maybe?) Though really, as long as the Hunger 10s are already tainting the action, maybe that's kind of redundant.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Am I reading this right? I don't see how the Cognitive Dissonance section on p168 could come into play for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 01-03-2020, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}